{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "09", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "20", "S": "25"}}, "news": [{"title": "Freehold relief in sight for Chandigarh\u2019s leasehold properties", "para": "The Ministry of Home Affairs is currently reviewing a proposal to convert leasehold properties to freehold status. This pivotal development emerges after extensive discussions among political figures and ministers. The Chandigarh administration, having secured the needed approvals, forwarded this proposal. It is anticipated that this change will enhance property values and stimulate investment within the city, along with providing updates on other property-related matters.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/freehold-relief-in-sight-for-chandigarhs-leasehold-properties/133063350?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-272616/133063350.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Registration opens for 460 plots in Lucknow development body's Anant Nagar", "para": "Online registration for 460 plots in Lucknow's Anant Nagar scheme is now open.  These plots, ranging from 112.5 to 200 square metres, will be allotted through a lottery.  The Anant Nagar scheme is being developed along Mohan Road with wide roads and green spaces.  LDA will also conduct a lottery for 407 housing units on August 14.  Previously, the authority allotted 75 flats in Park View and Aishbagh Square apartments.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/registration-opens-for-460-plots-in-lucknow-development-bodys-anant-nagar/133063254?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-263930/133063254.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Andhra Pradesh rolls out fresh incentives for IGBC-certified green projects", "para": "Andhra Pradesh has rolled out new concessions on development fees specifically tailored for green buildings. Developers of silver-rated projects will receive a five percent discount, while those achieving a gold rating can look forward to a ten percent reduction. Platinum-rated projects are rewarded handsomely with a fifteen percent concession.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/andhra-pradesh-rolls-out-fresh-incentives-for-igbc-certified-green-projects/133063128?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-111714/133063128.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}